cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite the versioned software release and its accompanying source-data package. Software and data have separate reuse terms."
type: software
title: "ArthroSkill-MC: occlusion-aware multimodal skill assessment in arthroscopy"
authors:
  - family-names: Xi
    given-names: Ning
version: 1.0-paper
date-released: '2026-10-27'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Irene-NingXi/ArthroSkill-MC'
url: 'https://github.com/Irene-NingXi/ArthroSkill-MC/releases/tag/v1.0-paper'
abstract: >-
  PyTorch implementation, current de-identified source tables, procedure-level
  evaluation and statistical reanalysis for a 196-procedure, three-centre
  arthroscopy benchmark. Includes the pinned official RGB-and-optical-flow
  SAIS integration. Software uses MIT; data reuse is governed by
  data/source_data/TERMS.md. Source recordings and fitted study weights are
  not included. A DOI must be added only after an archive assigns it.
keywords:
  - arthroscopy
  - surgical-skill-assessment
  - multimodal-learning
  - optical-flow
  - reproducibility
